      "writtenOn": "2015-11-03T18:36:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are S0ix and S3 support usually mutually exclusive? Will we normally want to support either one or the other?",
      "revId": "8a0f40a830ae314fbdf2fedf1845556a9e4e2316",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "760e462a_a372857e",
        "filename": "include/power.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000100
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-03T18:43:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We will need to support both at the same time as there may be situations where we go to S3 instead of S0ix.\n\nBut S0ix is likely here to stay, so we may not need to guard the basics with a CONFIG option.  We can always control the behavior by not configuring the GPIO for it on a board.",
      "parentUuid": "562a227b_ce7fd842",
      "revId": "8a0f40a830ae314fbdf2fedf1845556a9e4e2316",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "36204e91_546c85a0",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 510,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-02T20:47:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What if another power signal toggles at approximately the same time as your \"1 ms every 8s\" pulse? Then, you\u0027ll sample the periodic pulse, and maybe make a wrong conclusion about the actual power state?",
      "revId": "8a0f40a830ae314fbdf2fedf1845556a9e4e2316",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "765c8636_103505d4",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 510,
      "author": {
        "id": 1127214
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-03T00:49:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This periodic SLP_S0 pulse occurs only when S0ix state where SLP_S0 is asserted, unlike SLP_S3 which stays low when asserted.(this is due to unused PECI bus pin is grounded.).\nWhen SLP_S0 is de-asserted, there will be no more pulses.\n\nWhen other signals(SLP_S3 or S4) to be asserted, SLP_S0 is already de-asserted and it is unlikely for simultaneous signal changes.    \nAll these signal behaviour are controlled by PCH in SOC.",
      "parentUuid": "36204e91_546c85a0",
      "revId": "8a0f40a830ae314fbdf2fedf1845556a9e4e2316",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7643a650_5d72762f",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 510,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-03T18:36:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, it\u0027s not just a power signal toggle that can lead to misidentification of power state. Anything that wakes TASK_ID_CHIPSET can also cause it, right?\n\nMy suggestion is to create a variable that represents the debounced signal. The chipset task will deal with that variable only. Your ISR / deferred routine will deal with the actual signal and toggle the variable and wake the CHIPSET task when necessary.\n\nWe may need to introduce the concept of a power signal that\u0027s not actually a GPIO.",
      "parentUuid": "765c8636_103505d4",
      "revId": "8a0f40a830ae314fbdf2fedf1845556a9e4e2316",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "765c8636_5c039925",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 515,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-02T20:47:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The purpose of these two functions is to debounce the 1ms pulse every 8s, right? Do you really need a separate ISR to do this? For example, why not call your deferred routine from _power_handle_state? In any case, it\u0027s probably best to put this code in skylake.c, not here.",
      "revId": "8a0f40a830ae314fbdf2fedf1845556a9e4e2316",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5625c29e_fd68183b",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 515,
      "author": {
        "id": 1127214
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-03T00:49:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The purpose of debounce is not to wakeup chipset task when interrupt is not valid since chipset task produces messages(\"power state S0ix \u003d 0x1d...\") and this message prevents idles task from entering heavy sleep.( need at least 1 min quiet/no UART activity).\n\"_power_handle_state\" is called only when chipset tast wakes up. \n\nTo move S0 interrupt and its deferred call to skylake.c, \"power_update_signal()\" should be NOT \u0027static\u0027 inside common.c and defined in header file. Do you think if this change is OK to move S0 interrupt to skyale?",
      "parentUuid": "765c8636_5c039925",
      "revId": "8a0f40a830ae314fbdf2fedf1845556a9e4e2316",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "765c8636_a98db4e5",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 515,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-03T18:36:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this S0ix code going to apply to future chipsets, or is the implementation here mostly skylake-specific (especially the 1ms pulse every 8s)? If it\u0027s the second case then definitely we don\u0027t want the code in power/common.c. If it\u0027s the first case, maybe it makes sense to put the code here (or a new file power/s0ix.c maybe).\n\nI don\u0027t think we want to make power_update_signals non-static.",
      "parentUuid": "5625c29e_fd68183b",
      "revId": "8a0f40a830ae314fbdf2fedf1845556a9e4e2316",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "562a227b_835acc33",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 522,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-02T20:47:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not 1 * MSEC?",
      "revId": "8a0f40a830ae314fbdf2fedf1845556a9e4e2316",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "765c8636_f0ddd130",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 522,
      "author": {
        "id": 1127214
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-03T00:49:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since pulse width is 1 msec, checking SLP_S0 level should be after 1 msec to make sure if this rising edge is from invlaid 1 msec pulse or from valid power state change.",
      "parentUuid": "562a227b_835acc33",
      "revId": "8a0f40a830ae314fbdf2fedf1845556a9e4e2316",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
